This contains my vim and shell configuration. install.sh symlinks the files to their necessary locations. Beware, though, this overwrites any files that already sit at ~/.vimrc and ~/.vim/

For the shell in $SHELL (zsh or bash), install.sh also:
  - symlinks .zsh-aliases or .bash_aliases into ~ and sources it from ~/.zshrc or ~/.bashrc
  - zsh: enables git completion by adding compinit to ~/.zshrc
  - bash: downloads the latest git-completion.bash from the git repo to ~/.git-completion.bash and sources it from ~/.bashrc
